ss":"my"}],"gloss":"my"},{"surface":"கண்ணே","parts":[{"text":"கண்","lemma":"kaṇ","gloss":"eye"},{"text":"ஏ","lemma":"ē","gloss":"emphasis"}],"gloss":"eyes"},{"surface":"அவன்","parts":[{"text":"அவன்","lemma":"avaṉ","gloss":"his"}],"gloss":"his"},{"surface":"சொல்","parts":[{"text":"சொல்","lemma":"col","gloss":"word"}],"gloss":"words"}]},{"words":[{"surface":"கேட்டன","parts":[{"text":"கேள்","lemma":"kēḷ","gloss":"hear"},{"text":"ட்","lemma":"t","gloss":"past tense"},{"text":"அன","lemma":"aṉa","gloss":"neuter plural suffix"}],"gloss":"heard"},{"surface":"மன்","parts":[{"text":"மன்","lemma":"maṉ","gloss":"particle of past regret"}],"gloss":"indeed"},{"surface":"எம்","parts":[{"text":"எம்","lemma":"yām","gloss":"my"}],"gloss":"my"},{"surface":"செவியே","parts":[{"text":"செவி","lemma":"cevi","gloss":"ear"},{"text":"ஏ","lemma":"ē","gloss":"emphasis"}],"gloss":"ears"},{"surface":"மற்று","parts":[{"text":"மற்று","lemma":"maṟṟu","gloss":"but"}],"gloss":"but"},{"surface":"அவன்","parts":[{"text":"அவன்","lemma":"avaṉ","gloss":"his"}],"gloss":"his"}]},{"words":[{"surface":"மணப்பின்","parts":[{"text":"மணப்பு","lemma":"maṇappu","gloss":"union"},{"text":"இன்","lemma":"iṉ","gloss":"if"}],"gloss":"if united"},{"surface":"மாண்","parts":[{"text":"மாண்","lemma":"māṇ","gloss":"excellent"}],"gloss":"excellent"},{"surface":"நலம்","parts":[{"text":"நலம்","lemma":"nalam","gloss":"beauty"}],"gloss":"beauty"},{"surface":"எய்தி","parts":[{"text":"எய்தி","lemma":"eyti","gloss":"attaining"}],"gloss":"attaining"}]},{"words":[{"surface":"தணப்பின்","parts":[{"text":"தணப்பின்","lemma":"தணப்பின்","gloss":""}],"gloss":"","split_unverified":true},{"surface":"நெகிழ்பவெந்","parts":[{"text":"நெகிழ்பவெந்","lemma":"நெகிழ்பவெந்","gloss":""}],"gloss":"","split_unverified":true},{"surface":"தடமென்","parts":[{"text":"தடமென்","lemma":"தடமென்","gloss":""}],"gloss":"","split_unverified":true},{"surface":"றோளே","parts":[{"text":"றோளே","lemma":"றோளே","gloss":""}],"gloss":"","split_unverified":true}],"as_printed":true}],"literal":"What is this indeed, O friend? On the day when the tryst succeeded in the shade of the sand dune of the blooming-clustered Punnai tree in the seashore grove where birds chirp and ocean waves of ancient water sport, / my eyes indeed saw the lord, / my ears indeed heard his words, / but when united, attaining excellent beauty, / when separated, they become loose, my broad soft shoulders!","translation":"What is this, my friend? On the day we met at our tryst, in the shade of the sand dunes under the blooming clusters of the punnai tree, in the seaside grove where birds chirp and waves of the ancient sea sport, my eyes saw the lord of the shore, and my ears heard his words. But now, while they gain great beauty when we are together, my broad, soft shoulders waste away and grow thin whenever he departs.","modern":"தோழியே! இது என்ன விந்தை? பறவைகள் ஒலிக்கும் கடற்கரைச் சோலையில், பழமையான கடல் அலைகள் விளையாடும் மணல் மேட்டின் புன்னை மர நிழலில், எங்களது சந்திப்பு நிகழ்ந்த அன்று என் கண்கள் தலைவனைக் கண்டன; என் காதுகள் அவன் சொற்களைக் கேட்டன. ஆனால், அவன் கூடி இருக்கும்போது சிறந்த அழகைப் பெறும் என் பருத்த மென்மையான தோள்கள், அவன் பிரிந்து செல்லும்போது மெலிந்து தளர்கின்றனவே!","explanation":"The heroine is speaking to her close friend about her distress due to the hero's absence. She recalls the sweet day of their tryst under the shade of the blooming punnai tree on the sand dunes of the seashore. During that meeting, her eyes saw him and her ears heard his comforting words, which brought her great joy. However, she points out a painful paradox: her shoulders, which flourish and look beautiful when they are united, immediately waste away and grow thin when he is away. The coastal landscape (Neytal tiṇai), with its crashing waves and chirping birds, reflects the turbulent emotions of longing and separation. Key words like 'maṇappin' (if united) and 'taṇappin' (if separated) highlight the contrast between the joy of union and the physical toll of separation.","model":"gemini-3.5-flash"}}